    "narrative": "The centerpiece of today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 87.14 against Sugano. The combination of a favorable 4.80 xERA matchup and a slow-delivery pitcher creates a premium environment for his stolen base upside, further bolstered by his placement in the #2 hole. Similarly, **James Wood** provides high-octane production (68.66) as a leadoff hitter against Elder; he is a priority play given the 100% stolen base probability against this battery and his strong xwOBA. **Tyler Soderstrom** also earns a strong nod (73.03) against Buehler, benefiting from a significant platoon advantage and a high-floor matchup that makes him a vital anchor for our middle-of-the-order production.\n\nOn the bench, the decision to sit **Dalton Rushing** (38.26) was the most nuanced cut of the day. While he offers solid raw potential, the combination of a daunting 3.08 xERA matchup and a bottom-tier batting order assignment (#8) pushed him below our 40.0 efficiency threshold. Conversely, we are keeping **Brice Turang** in the lineup despite a lower base projection; his score is artificially supported by his position as an elite stolen base threat facing a slow-delivery pitcher, proving that our roster prioritization remains squarely focused on maintaining dominance in our scarcest category. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a necessary start in the UTIL slot to capture his platoon edge against Gilbert, though we are monitoring the 3.03 xERA matchup closely as it represents the toughest SP skill hurdle for any of our active hitters today.",
